Our episodes deal with serious and often distressing incidents. If you feel at any time you need support, please contact your local crisis centre. For suggested phone numbers for confidential support, please see the show notes for this episode on your app or on our website. Due to the nature of this crime, K-Spile has elected to change the names of several individuals featured in this episode. In April of 2004, teenager Laura Fletcher had recently celebrated her 18th birthday. She was in the final months of her senior year of high school and was set to graduate as one of the top 10 students in her class. An avid painter and photographer, Laura took advanced art lessons to further her creative skills. But her main ambition was to study pre-med at the University of Louisville in her home state of Kentucky so she could later attend medical school.
我们的节目涉及严重且往往令人痛苦的事件。如果您在任何时候觉得自己需要支持，请联系您当地的危机中心。有关获得保密支持的建议电话号码，请查看您应用上或我们网站上本期节目的shownotes。由于这起犯罪的性质，K-Spile选择更改本期节目中几位当事人的姓名。2004年4月，十几岁的劳拉·弗莱彻刚刚庆祝了她18岁的生日。她当时正处于高中高三的最后几个月，并准备以班级前10名的优异成绩毕业。作为一个热爱绘画和摄影的人，劳拉上了高级美术课来提升自己的创意技能。但她最大的志向是在家乡肯塔基州的路易斯维尔大学攻读医学预科，以便日后进入医学院深造。

3
00:01:45.000 --> 00:02:51.000
Laura's reputation for being responsible and well-behaved extended outside of school hours. She attended church regularly and had previously been a Girl Scout. When her mother's health issues led to her losing her job, Laura offered to help support her family. In January 2004, she got a part-time job at a local McDonald's fast food restaurant near her home in Mount Washington. Earning $6.35 an hour, Laura was a reliable employee who was always willing to help out by taking on extra shifts. At around 4.45pm on Friday, April 9, Laura was preparing to head home after finishing an afternoon shift. Before she left, her manager asked if she could stay a little longer to cover for another employee who had just called in sick. Friday evenings were always busy and the restaurant couldn't afford to be understaffed.
劳拉负责任和表现良好的名声不仅体现在学校。她经常去教堂，以前还是一名女童子军。当母亲的健康问题导致母亲失业时，劳拉主动提出帮助养家糊口。2004年1月，她在离位于华盛顿山的家不远的一家当地麦当劳快餐店找到了一份兼职工作。劳拉的时薪为6.35美元，是一名可靠的员工，总是乐意通过多上几个班来帮忙。4月9日星期五下午4点45分左右，劳拉刚上完下午的班，正准备回家。在她离开之前，她的经理问她是否能多待一会儿，顶替一个刚刚打电话说生病的员工。星期五的晚上总是很忙，餐厅经不起人手不足的折腾。

4
00:02:51.000 --> 00:04:29.000
Laura would only have to stay until someone else could be found to work the entire shift. Happy to help and eager for the chance to earn a little extra money, Laura agreed to continue working. McDonald's employees who worked a double shift were given a free meal to tide them over, so Laura took a short break to eat before returning behind the counter. Also working that night was 51-year-old Donna Summers, one of the restaurant's assistant managers. Like Laura, Summers was relatively new to the franchise. She had only been working there for about 8 months. Just as Laura returned to serving customers, the restaurant's phone rang at 4.56pm. Summers answered it. On the other end was a man who identified himself as a police officer named Officer Scott. Officer Scott explained that he had McDonald's corporate on another line, as well as Lisa Siddons, the store's manager.
劳拉只需要呆到能找到其他人来上整个班为止。劳拉很乐意帮忙，也很渴望有赚点外快机会，于是她同意继续工作。上双班的麦当劳员工可以得到一顿免费餐食以度过这段时间，因此劳拉在回到柜台后面之前休息了一会儿吃东西。当晚也在工作的还有51岁的唐娜·萨默斯，她是餐厅的助理经理之一。和劳拉一样，萨默斯对这家连锁店来说也比较新。她才在那里工作了大约8个月。就在劳拉回去为顾客服务时，餐厅的电话在下午4点56分响了。萨默斯接了电话。电话那头是一个自称是名叫斯科特警官的男子。斯科特警官解释说，他另一条线路上有麦当劳公司的人，还有该店的经理丽莎·西多恩斯。

5
00:04:29.000 --> 00:05:35.000
He was calling because a child who had been in the restaurant earlier had her coin purse stolen. The culprit was believed to be one of Summers employees. He provided a physical description of the suspect, young, white and female, with a petite build and dark hair. She was wearing a McDonald's uniform. Officer Scott also described a tie that the suspect was wearing. Summers immediately thought of Laura Fletcher. Even though her work record was exemplary, she'd fit the suspect's description perfectly. While leaving Officer Scott waiting on the phone, Summers found Laura and asked her to accompany her to the manager's office at the back of the restaurant. The small, cramped room had a tiled floor with a desk and a countertop running against opposing walls. Their surfaces were crowded with a computer and various items of stationery.
他打电话是因为一个早些时候在餐厅里的小孩的零币钱包被偷了。罪魁祸首被认为是萨默斯的员工之一。他提供了嫌疑人的体貌特征：年轻、白人、女性，身材娇小，留着深色头发。她穿着麦当劳制服。斯科特警官还描述了嫌疑人系的一条领带。萨默斯立刻想到了劳拉·弗莱彻。尽管她的工作记录无可挑剔，但她完全符合嫌疑人的描述。在让斯科特警官在电话那头等候的同时，萨默斯找到了劳拉，并请她陪自己去餐厅后面的经理办公室。这个狭小拥挤的房间里铺着瓷砖地板，一张桌子和一个操作台沿着相对的墙壁延伸。它们的表面挤满了电脑和各种文具用品。

6
00:05:35.000 --> 00:06:23.000
A filing cabinet sat to one side and boxes were stacked beneath the bench top. Perched up high in the ceiling was a CCTV camera. Summers led Laura into the manager's office before locking the door behind them. She then informed Laura that a police officer had accused her of robbing a customer. Shocked, Laura immediately protested her innocence, telling her manager, Donna, I've never done anything wrong. I could never steal. Summers responded that a police officer had described Laura as the person responsible. Officer Scott was still waiting on the phone.
一个文件柜放在一侧，长椅下方堆放着箱子。天花板高处安装着一个闭路电视摄像头。萨默斯把劳拉领进经理办公室，然后把门锁上。接着她告知劳拉，一名警官指控她抢劫了一名顾客。劳拉大吃一惊，立即抗议自己的清白，对经理唐娜说：“我从来没有做错过任何事。我绝不可能偷东西。”萨默斯回答说，一名警官描述劳拉就是那个应该负责的人。斯科特警官还在电话那头等着。

7
00:06:23.000 --> 00:07:07.000
Summers switched between speaking to him and Laura. Officer Scott informed Summers that Laura had two choices. She could either submit to a search for the stolen purse then and there, or she could wait until an officer came to arrest her and undergo a search at the police station. Upon learning of her options, Laura started to cry and to beg to be taken to the police station so the matter could be cleared up there. Summers handed the phone to Laura, who spoke to Officer Scott herself. After doing so, Laura agreed to be searched on the spot.
萨默斯在与他和劳拉交谈之间切换。斯科特警官通知萨默斯，劳拉有两个选择。要么她当场接受搜查以找回被偷的钱包，要么她等警察来逮捕她并在警察局接受搜查。得知自己的选择后，劳拉哭了起来，并哀求带她去警察局，以便在那里把事情弄清楚。萨默斯把电话递给劳拉，劳拉亲自和斯科特警官对话。在此之后，劳拉同意当场接受搜查。

