00:09:48.000 --> 00:10:46.000
Summers told Officer Scott that she also needed to get back to work. He requested that she find a male employee to watch over Laura until police arrived. Summers summoned Jason Bradley, a 27-year-old cook. She left him in the office with Laura and the telephone while she went back to her managerial duties in the restaurant. Laura held the apron against the front of her body as Jason faced away from her and spoke to Officer Scott. Upon learning that Laura was wearing nothing but an apron, Officer Scott told Jason to remove it and describe her body to him. This made Jason angry. After speaking with the officer for several minutes, he stormed out of the office and told Summers the entire matter was a lot of BS.
萨默斯告诉斯科特警官她也需要回去工作。他要求她找一个男员工来看守劳拉，直到警察到达。萨默斯叫来了27岁的厨师杰森·布拉德利。她把他和劳拉以及电话一起留在办公室里，自己则回到了餐厅履行经理职责。劳拉用围裙挡在身体前面，而杰森则背对她与斯科特警官交谈。得知劳拉只穿着一条围裙时，斯科特警官让杰森脱掉它并向他描述她的身体。这惹恼了杰森。与警官交谈了几分钟后，他冲出办公室，告诉萨默斯整件事全是一堆废话。

12
00:10:46.000 --> 00:11:39.000
He flatly told her that he wanted no part of it before resuming his work in the kitchen. Summers didn't understand what Jason was upset about, so she resumed control of the phone. By now, it had been 40 minutes since she had answered Officer Scott's call. Summers explained that there was nobody else available to keep watch over Laura. In response, Officer Scott asked, Are you married? Summers giggled and informed the officer that she was actually engaged. When asked if she trusted her fiance, Summers said she did. Officer Scott queried whether Summers' fiance would be able to come to the restaurant to keep an eye on Laura.
他直截了当地告诉她，他不想参与其中，然后回到厨房继续工作。萨默斯不明白杰森为什么生气，于是她重新接管了电话。到目前为止，距离她接听斯科特警官的电话已经过去40分钟了。萨默斯解释说，没有其他人可以留下来看守劳拉。作为回应，斯科特警官问：“你结婚了吗？”萨默斯咯咯笑着告诉警官，她其实已经订婚了。当被问及她是否信任未婚夫时，萨默斯说她信任。斯科特警官追问萨默斯的未婚夫是否能来餐厅看守劳拉。

13
00:11:39.000 --> 00:12:31.000
Summers agreed to call him and ask. Walter Nix Jr. was a 42-year-old father of two who worked as an exterminator. A churchgoing man who coached youth baseball teams, he was considered an upstanding member of the community. He and Donna Summers had only recently gotten engaged. Shortly before 6pm, Summers used her cell phone to call Nix. She explained that an employee was being investigated for theft and dealing drugs. When asked if he could help by keeping watch over her until police arrived, Nix agreed. He arrived at the McDonald's soon afterwards.
