51
00:50:58.000 --> 00:52:07.000
Stewart's legal team used this testimony to theorize that Laura had orchestrated the attack as a scam to obtain a large sum of money. Laura's attorney told the media that the accusation that her client was involved in her own assault was, quote, a ridiculous and desperate suggestion. In his closing argument, Stewart's lawyer told the jury that his client was nothing more than a fall guy for police, stating, They came to a conclusion, then went about looking for facts to support it. On Tuesday, October 31, the jury of six men and six women retired to consider their verdict. They returned to court less than two hours later. David Stewart closed his eyes and bowed his head as a not guilty verdict was read aloud. The jury had acquitted him of all charges.
斯图尔特的法律团队利用这一证词推论说，劳拉策划了这次袭击，是一场企图骗取巨额金钱的骗局。劳拉的律师向媒体表示，指控她的当事人参与了自己的遇袭是一项“荒谬且绝望的猜测”。在结案陈词中，斯图尔特的律师对陪审团说，他的当事人不过是替警方背锅的牺牲品，并宣称：“他们先得出一个结论，然后到处寻找支持该结论的事实。”10月31日星期二，由六名男性和六名女性组成的陪审团退庭商议他们的裁决。不到两个小时后，他们返回法庭。当宣读无罪判决时，大卫·斯图尔特闭上眼睛，低下了头。陪审团判定他所有指控不成立。

52
00:52:07.000 --> 00:53:06.000
When he was permitted to leave the courtroom, Stewart left in silence with his family. He refused to speak with the waiting press. Stewart's attorney celebrated the acquittal and told journalists it was the result of what evidence the prosecution had. But prosecutor Mike Mann said he was certain police had found the right person. He pointed out that there had been no further strip search scam calls since Stewart was arrested two and a half years earlier. Law enforcement agencies in other jurisdictions across the country had been waiting to see how the trial against Stewart panned out. For many of the scam calls that occurred prior to Laura Fletcher's assault, the only crime Stewart could have been charged with was a misdemeanor. Extradition from another state would not have been permitted under these circumstances.
当他被允许离开法庭时，斯图尔特和他的家人默默地离开了。他拒绝与等候在外的记者交谈。斯图尔特的律师为无罪释放进行庆祝，并告诉记者这是检方证据不足的结果。但检察官迈克·曼恩（Mike Mann）表示，他确信警方找到了正确的人。他指出，自从两年半前斯图尔特被捕以来，就再也没有发生过针对此类搜身诈骗的电话。全国其他司法管辖区的执法机构一直都在观望针对斯图尔特的审判结果会如何。对于在劳拉·弗莱彻遇袭之前发生的许多诈骗电话，斯图尔特唯一能被起诉的罪名只是轻罪。在这种情况下，不允许从其他州进行引渡。

53
00:53:06.000 --> 00:54:19.000
After the jury in Bullock County, Kentucky found Stewart not guilty, there were no further charges brought against him for any of the other cases throughout the United States, of which there were more than 70. Laura Fletcher was seeking more than $200 million in damages from McDonald's. She was suing the then $59 billion corporation for assault, battery, sexual harassment, and failure to train. Her attorneys alleged that McDonald's failed to protect Laura by neglecting to warn staff about the ongoing hoaxes. The company had been aware of the issue for at least two years prior to her ordeal. There had been about 30 other scam calls to McDonald's restaurants throughout the country that involved girls and young women being assaulted and forced to strip in front of others. 12 of these incidents resulted in the corporation being taken to court in four different states. Settlements had been reached in all of these cases.
在肯塔基州布利特县的陪审团裁定斯图尔特无罪后，美国各地发生的所有其他类似案件（共有70多起）再也没有对其实施任何进一步的指控。劳拉·弗莱彻正向麦当劳寻求超过2亿美元的赔偿。她起诉这家当时价值590亿美元的公司存在故意伤害、殴打、性骚扰以及未能履行培训职责。她的律师指控麦当劳未能通过警告员工注意正在发生的骗局来保护劳拉。该公司在她的苦难发生前至少两年就已经意识到了这个问题。全美各地曾发生过大约30起针对麦当劳餐厅的类似诈骗电话，涉及女孩和年轻女性遭到袭击并被迫在他人面前脱衣。其中12起事件导致该公司在四个不同的州被推上法庭。所有这些案件均已达成和解。

54
00:54:19.000 --> 00:55:13.000
Laura's was the first to proceed the trial. In addition to suing McDonald's, Laura's suit named assistant managers Donna Summers and Kim Dockery as well as David Stewart. Stewart responded with a letter that read in part, I received your notice but I'm in no way responsible. I feel bad for your loss because I am a victim as well. I lost my job, my home, and my car all over something I did not do. Louisville newspaper The Courier Journal revealed that Florida property records indicated Stewart had not lost the trailer where he resided, but he had deeded it to his wife for $100.
劳拉的案子是第一个进入审判程序的。除了起诉麦当劳外，劳拉的诉讼还点名了副经理唐娜·萨默斯、金·多克里（Kim Dockery）以及大卫·斯图尔特。斯图尔特回信写道：“我收到了你的通知，但我绝不负任何责任。我为你的损失感到难过，因为我也是受害者。我失去了工作、我的家和我的车，这一切都是因为一件我根本没做过的事。”路易斯维尔报纸《信使报》（The Courier Journal）披露，佛罗里达州的财产记录显示，斯图尔特并没有失去他居住的拖车房，而是以100美元的价格把它过户给了他的妻子。

55
00:55:13.000 --> 00:56:22.000
Donna Summers filed a cross complaint against McDonald's for $50 million. She claimed that they had failed to warn store managers about the hoaxer. Her case would be presented alongside Laura's. In response, McDonald's asserted that Laura was the victim of a malicious hoax by individuals not representing McDonald's. They blamed Summers and Walter Nix for the incident as well as Laura herself. McDonald's insisted that all three should have realized the call was a scam. They also stated that strip searches had been against company policy since 2001 and Summers should have known this as it was mentioned in the store manual. After a lengthy discovery period in which 57 depositions were obtained from more than 40 witnesses, the trial commenced in the Bullitt County Circuit Court on September 10, 2007.
唐娜·萨默斯对麦当劳提起了5000万美元的反诉。她声称麦当劳未能警告店长注意骗局。她的案子将与劳拉的案子合并审理。作为回应，麦当劳坚称劳拉是由不代表麦当劳的个人所策划的恶毒骗局的受害者。他们将这起事件归咎于萨默斯、沃尔特·尼克斯以及劳拉本人。麦当劳坚称，这三个人本都应该意识到这通电话是个骗局。他们还表示，自2001年以来，搜身检查就一直是公司政策所禁止的，萨默斯理应知道这一点，因为门店手册中已经提到了这一点。在经过漫长的证据开示期（从40多名证人那里获得了57份证词）之后，该案于2007年9月10日在布利特县巡回法院正式开庭审理。

56
00:56:22.000 --> 00:57:37.000
McDonald's had withheld 16 boxes of evidence regarding prior hoaxes from the plaintiffs on the grounds that handing them over would violate attorney-client privilege. A judge forced them to surrender the material the evening before the trial began. The case had received national attention and consequently, it was difficult to find jurors who were unfamiliar with it. Out of 110 potential jurors, less than a dozen had never heard of the case before. Eventually, the pool was narrowed down to 15, including three alternates. The first witness for the plaintiffs was McDonald's US security manager who testified via video link about the other scam calls the company received between 1994 and 2004. He said that the company realized there was a problem in 2001 after franchises began reporting the incident. A top attorney for McDonald's conceded that the warning about the calls was inadequate.
麦当劳以交出这些材料会违反律师与客户的特权为由，向原告隐瞒了16箱关于以往骗局的证据。法官在审判开始的前一天晚上强迫他们交出了这些材料。该案件受到了全国范围的关注，因此很难找到对它完全不了解的陪审员。在110名潜在陪审员中，只有不到十几人以前从未听说过这个案子。最终，陪审团名单缩小到15人，其中包括3名候补陪审员。原告的第一位证人是麦当劳美国安全经理，他通过视频连线作证，讲述了该公司在1994年至2004年期间收到的其他诈骗电话。他说，在各个加盟店开始报告此类事件后，公司在2001年意识到了问题的存在。麦当劳的一位高级律师承认，针对这些电话的警告是不够充分的。

57
00:57:37.000 --> 00:59:07.000
They said employees weren't told about the scam calls because the corporation didn't want to discourage them from cooperating with the genuine law enforcement officers. Expert witness Barry Collins, who was a social psychologist from the University of California, told the court that all of the calls were likely made by a single perpetrator as they all shared an identical method and signature. He said that the perpetrator was someone who, quote, enjoyed being in control and ruining people's lives and derived some sexual pleasure from his exploits. Professor Collins explained that managers who fell for the scam calls were won over gradually. The caller would dish out compliments and commendation to encourage the managers and assure them that they were doing the right thing. His trivial requests slowly escalated to more outrageous demands. Collins testified that if McDonald's had been serious about putting a stop to the incidents, then they could have done so as they had intensive training programs set up on a range of other matters. A psychiatrist who had examined Laura testified that she would suffer post-traumatic stress disorder for the rest of her life.
他们说，之所以不把诈骗电话的情况告诉员工，是因为公司不想打消他们配合真正执法人员工作的积极性。来自加利福尼亚大学的社会心理学家、专家证人巴里·柯林斯（Barry Collins）向法庭表示，所有这些电话很可能都是由同一个作案人打的，因为它们都具有完全相同的作案手法和特征。他说，作案者是一个“喜欢掌控一切、毁掉别人生活，并从中获得某种性快感”的人。柯林斯教授解释说，那些落入骗局陷阱的经理是一点点被说服的。打电话的人会抛出恭维和表扬，以鼓励经理并向他们保证他们正在做正确的事情。他那些微不足道的请求慢慢升级为更加离谱的要求。柯林斯作证说，如果麦当劳真的认真想要制止这些事件，他们完全可以做到，因为他们在其他一系列问题上已经建立了一套密集的培训项目。曾为劳拉做过检查的精神病医生作证说，她在余生中都将遭受创伤后应激障碍（PTSD）的折磨。

58
00:59:07.000 --> 01:00:34.000
She was also fearful of strangers and struggled with intimacy. On Thursday, September 20, Laura Fletcher began what would end up being six hours of testimony. She broke down in tears as she discussed the assault and its long-standing impact on her, including her struggle to conceal her pain, shame and humiliation from friends and family. When asked where she thought responsibility for the incident lay, she replied, McDonald's. When it was time for Donna Summers to take the stand, she wept and admitted that she had considered taking her own life due to ongoing feelings of guilt. Summers said she prayed for Laura daily, but acknowledged that she hadn't asked enough questions when the scammer called. She insisted that McDonald's had never trained her on the matter, or made it clear that strip searches were a violation of company policy. When asked why she left her fiance alone with a naked teenager, Summers said she had believed Nix was kind and gentle, and said she would have trusted him with her own daughter.
她还对陌生人感到恐惧，并且在亲密关系上苦苦挣扎。9月20日星期四，劳拉·弗莱彻开始作证，最终这证词持续了足足六个小时。在谈到袭击事件及其对她造成的长期影响时，她失声痛哭，包括她极力向朋友和家人隐瞒痛苦、羞耻和屈辱的挣扎。当被问及她认为这起事件的责任在谁时，她回答道：“麦当劳。”轮到唐娜·萨默斯走上证人席时，她哭着承认，由于内心的负罪感挥之不去，她曾考虑过自杀。萨默斯说她每天都为劳拉祈祷，但也承认骗子打电话来时她没有问足够多的问题。她坚称麦当劳从未就此事对她进行过培训，也没有明确表示搜身检查违反了公司政策。当被问及为什么把未婚夫单独和一个赤身裸体的十几岁女孩留在房间里时，萨默斯说她当时相信尼克斯是个善良温柔的人，并表示她甚至敢把自己的亲生女儿托付给他。

59
01:00:34.000 --> 01:02:03.000
In their opening statement, McDonald's blamed Donna Summers for the assault by saying that if she hadn't violated company policy by bringing Nix into the manager's office, then it wouldn't have happened. The company denied the assertion that they had not sufficiently warned staff about the scammer. A few days before Laura's assault on April 9, 2004, a voice message about the calls was sent to McDonald's managers all over the country. One of the company's human resources executives testified that Donna Summers exercised poor judgment over a long period of time, and noted that she didn't have authority to remove Laura's clothing, or invite a non-employee to the back of the restaurant. A psychiatrist and psychologist who were paid as expert witnesses by McDonald's contradicted the plaintiff's psychiatrist by saying that Laura's trauma was not permanent. One even suggested that she had grown stronger as a result of her assault. The defense also argued that Laura now had a happy life with a long-term boyfriend and a well-paid job at a legal firm. Lisa Siddons, the Mount Washington McDonald's manager, appeared on behalf of the defense.
在开案陈词中，麦当劳将袭击归咎于唐娜·萨默斯，称如果她不是把尼克斯带进经理办公室从而违反了公司政策，这一切就不会发生。该公司否认了他们没有充分警告员工注意骗子的说法。在2004年4月9日劳拉遭遇袭击几天前，一条关于这些电话的语音消息被发送给了全国各地的麦当劳经理。该公司的一位人力资源高管作证说，唐娜·萨默斯在很长一段时间里做出了糟糕的判断，并指出她既没有权力脱掉劳拉的衣服，也没有权力邀请非员工进入餐厅后台。麦当劳花钱聘请的精神病医生和心理学家作为专家证人，与原告的精神病医生唱反调，称劳拉的创伤并非永久性的。其中一人甚至暗示，她在遭遇袭击后变得更坚强了。辩方还辩称，劳拉现在与一个长期交往的男友过着幸福的生活，并在一家律师事务所拥有高薪工作。山华盛顿麦当劳的经理丽莎·西登斯作为辩方证人出庭。

60
01:02:03.000 --> 01:03:21.000
She said she had received the company's voicemail about the scammer, but hadn't passed it on to her assistant managers because she didn't think it was important. She also added, quote, Anyone dumb enough to fall for it shouldn't be a manager at McDonald's. On cross-examination, Lisa accepted that the voicemail had been vague. It merely referred to a caller asking for employees to be detained, and to mention nothing about strip searches. When asked if she would have treated the voicemail more seriously, had she known what sorts of abuses the caller was demanding, Lisa answered yes, and burst into tears. Lisa had worked for McDonald's since 1981, but said she was unfamiliar with its policy barring strip searches, and consequently couldn't have told her subordinates about it. It emerged that the company had never trained anybody on the policy. It was one of many listed in a 1000-page manual.
她说她收到了公司关于骗子的语音留言，但没有将其转告给她的副经理，因为她认为这不重要。她还补充说：“任何笨到会相信这种把戏的人都不配当麦当劳的经理。”在交叉盘问中，丽莎承认那条语音留言确实很含糊。它只是提及一个来电者要求拘留员工，完全没有提到搜身。当被问及如果她知道来电者要求的是何种虐待行为，她是否会对该语音留言采取更严肃的态度时，丽莎回答说会，并当场失声痛哭。丽莎自1981年起就在麦当劳工作，但她说她并不熟悉禁止搜身的政策，因此不可能将此事告知下属。事实证明，公司从未就这项政策对任何人进行过培训。它只是写在一本长达1000页的手册里的众多条目之一。

61
01:03:21.000 --> 01:04:37.000
The trial concluded after four weeks. The jury of eight women and four men were given 31 pages of instructions and 12 possible verdicts to consider. After deliberating for 13 hours, the jury found in favour of Laura's suit. They assigned half of the blame for her assault to the scammer and the other half to McDonald's. Laura was awarded a total of $6.1 million. This included $1.1 million in compensatory damages and $5 million in punitive damages. The jury attached a note to their verdict imploring McDonald's to offer more employee training on sexual harassment and scam calls. It was later revealed that the jury had taken so long deliberating because they had been unable to agree on how much money Laura should receive. One juror wanted to award her $100 million, while another wanted to give her just $1. The jury also awarded $1.1 million to Donna Summers.
审判在四周后结束。由八名女性和四名男性组成的陪审团收到了31页的指示和12种可能的裁决供他们考虑。经过13个小时的审议，陪审团裁定劳拉胜诉。他们将劳拉遇袭的一半责任归咎于骗子，另一半归咎于麦当劳。劳拉总共获得了610万美元的赔偿。其中包括110万美元的补偿性赔偿和500万美元的惩罚性赔偿。陪审团在裁决书附言中恳求麦当劳为员工提供更多关于性骚扰和诈骗电话的培训。后来有消息透露，陪审团之所以商议了这么久，是因为他们无法就劳拉应该获得多少金钱赔偿达成一致。一名陪审员希望判给她1亿美元，而另一名陪审员只想给她1美元。陪审团还判给唐娜·萨默斯110万美元。

62
01:04:37.000 --> 01:05:52.000
Kim Dockery, the other assistant manager who had been on duty at the time of Laura's assault, was exonerated of any responsibility. Laura burst into tears upon hearing the verdict and hugged her mother and grandparents. She also embraced Donna Summers and the two expressed their happiness for each other. Laura later told the press that she planned to use the money to go to law school as her original college plans had been derailed by her assault. Her lawyer described the verdict as a complete rejection of McDonald's claim that they bore no responsibility to Laura or other employees who had been victims of the strip search scams. Donna Summers told the media, It was never about the money. It was about getting the truth out that McDonald's knew all along what was going on. This was a complete vindication. McDonald's issued a statement that they would be considering whether or not to appeal the finding and noted,
金·多克里是劳拉遇袭时在场的另一位副经理，她被宣告无罪并免除了所有责任。劳拉听到裁决后失声痛哭，拥抱了她的母亲和祖父母。她还拥抱了唐娜·萨默斯，两人为彼此感到高兴。劳拉后来告诉媒体，她计划用这笔钱去读法学院，因为她最初的大学计划因那次遇袭而毁了。她的律师将该裁决描述为对麦当劳“他们对劳拉或其他作为搜身骗局受害者的员工不承担任何责任”这一说法的彻底否定。唐娜·萨默斯告诉媒体：“这从来都不是为了钱。这是为了把真相说出来——麦当劳从一开始就知道发生了什么。这是一种彻底的平反。”麦当劳发表声明称，他们将考虑是否对裁决提出上诉，并指出：

63
01:05:52.000 --> 01:07:48.000
As we've stated previously, this malicious hoax was perpetrated by individuals who do not represent our brand. What happened to Laura Fletcher was wrong and should never happen to anyone. McDonald's soon lodged an appeal. More than two years later, the Kentucky Court of Appeals ruled that they were upholding the jury's decision. A three-judge panel found that McDonald's legal department had been fully aware of the scammer, but made a conscious decision not to train or warn employees or managers about the calls. Despite upholding the decision, the judges deemed that the jury's sum awarded to Donna Summers had been excessive. Her payout was reduced from $1.1 million to $500,000. McDonald's was also ordered to pay a further $2.4 million in attorney fees for Laura. Laura, who had since become a mother, did not attend the appeal in person. Instead, one of her lawyers spoke to the media on her behalf stating that she was thrilled to learn of the verdict. McDonald's then decided to appeal the decision at Kentucky's Supreme Court. In 2010, while this petition was still pending, Laura settled with the company for an undisclosed amount, and McDonald's withdrew their second appeal. The case has drawn comparisons to a famous experiment conducted in the early 1960s by Yale University social psychologist Stanley Milgram.
“正如我们之前所说，这场恶毒的骗局是由不代表我们品牌的个人所策划的。发生在劳拉·弗莱彻身上的事情是错误的，绝不应该发生在使用我们品牌的任何人身上。”麦当劳不久便提起了上诉。两年多后，肯塔基州上诉法院裁定维持陪审团的决定。由三名法官组成的小组裁定，麦当劳的法律部门完全清楚骗子的存在，但却做出有意识的决定，不培训或警告员工或经理防范这些电话。尽管维持了原判，法官认为陪审团判给唐娜·萨默斯的金额过高。她的赔偿金从110万美元减至50万美元。麦当劳还被命令支付劳拉另外240万美元的律师费。此后已为人母的劳拉没有亲自出席上诉。相反，她的一位律师代表她向媒体发言，称她得知裁决结果后欣喜若狂。随后，麦当劳决定向肯塔基州最高法院对该判决提起上诉。2010年，在上诉仍在审理期间，劳拉与该公司达成了一笔未公开金额的和解，麦当劳也撤回了他们的第二次上诉。这起案件让人联想起20世纪60年代初由耶鲁大学社会心理学家斯坦利·米尔格拉姆（Stanley Milgram）进行的一项著名实验。

64
01:07:48.000 --> 01:09:12.000
In the experiment, Professor Milgram told his subjects that he was researching learning. What he was really studying was people's willingness to obey authority. Participants were asked to administer electric shocks at an ever-increasing voltage to another individual whenever that person answered a question incorrectly. The individuals on the receiving ends of the shocks were in fact actors who were not harmed at all. The experiment found that the majority of participants were willing to administer the electric shocks, even if they felt extremely upset about having to do so. In 1971, Stanford University Professor Philip Zimbardo carried out a similar study, which came to be known as the Stanford Prison Experiment. His college student participants were split into two groups and were either assigned the role of a prison guard or an inmate. Professor Zimbardo's aim was to investigate the psychological effects of perceived power. The students embraced their roles, and the guards soon became authoritative and alarmingly abusive towards the inmates.
在这项实验中，米尔格拉姆教授告诉他的受试者他正在研究学习过程。而他真正研究的其实是人们服从权威的意愿。当另一个人回答问题错误时，参与者被要求向其施加电压不断升高的电击。接受电击的那些人实际上是由演员扮演的，根本没有受到任何伤害。实验发现，大多数参与者都愿意实施电击，即便他们为此感到极其苦恼。1971年，斯坦福大学教授菲利普·津巴多（Philip Zimbardo）进行了类似的研究，也就是后来为人熟知的“斯坦福监狱实验”。他招募的大学生参与者被分成两组，分别扮演狱警或囚犯的角色。津巴多教授的目的是调查人们对感知权力的心理影响。学生们很快就进入了角色，狱警们也变得极具权威性，并对囚犯们进行了令人震惊的虐待。

